    'privacy' => [
        'title' => 'Privacy Policy',
        'intro' => 'This Policy explains how :brand (“Kopafasta”, “we”, “us”) processes personal data for microfinance membership, lending, payments, and related services under the Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA) of the United Republic of Tanzania (Cap. 44) and related regulations — including the Personal Data Protection (Personal Data Collection and Processing) Regulations, 2023 and the Personal Data Protection (Complaints Settlement Procedures) Regulations, 2023.',
        'sections' => [
            ['Who we are (data controller)', 'We are the data controller for borrower, guarantor, group-member, and visitor accounts on the Kopafasta digital lending platform operated by :brand. Where a licensed processor acts only on our documented instructions (for example hosting, SMS, payments, or identity/credit checks), that party is a data processor under the PDPA. Contact for privacy requests: :email.'],
            ['Scope and application', 'This Policy applies when you visit our website, register, pay a membership fee, complete KYC (including NIDA and face verification), apply for or guarantee a loan, repay, use USSD/SMS/in-app messages, or otherwise use Kopafasta channels. It should be read with our Terms of Service, AML/KYC notice, Complaints policy, and any product-specific consents you accept in the app.'],
            ['PDPA principles we follow', 'In line with section 5 of the PDPA and the Collection and Processing Regulations, 2023, we design processing around: lawfulness and fairness; a specific, disclosed purpose; collection limited to what is necessary and proportionate; accuracy and timely correction; security appropriate to the risk (including for sensitive data); retention only as long as needed for the purpose or law; and respect for your rights as a data subject. Where consent is the basis, we aim for clear, understandable consent and a practical way to withdraw it for future processing.'],
            ['Legal basis (PDPA)', 'We process personal data where necessary to perform a contract with you (membership, loans, repayments), to comply with legal obligations (KYC/AML, Bank of Tanzania requirements, credit reporting, and other applicable law), with your consent where required (e.g. biometric face capture and optional marketing), and for legitimate interests that do not override your rights (fraud prevention, platform security, service improvement that does not involve selling your data).'],
            ['Sensitive personal data', 'Face verification images and related biometric identifiers are treated as sensitive personal data under the PDPA. We process them only with your prior consent for identity verification and underwriting, or where another PDPA exception applies (e.g. legal compliance). You may withdraw consent for future biometric capture; withdrawal does not affect processing already lawfully completed. Where practicable, sensitive data is stored with stronger access controls and kept separate from general profile fields.'],
            ['Personal data we collect', 'Depending on the product and your role (borrower, guarantor, group member, or partner), we may collect: identity and contact details (name, phone, email, address, date of birth, gender, next of kin); national ID / NIDA numbers and card images; face verification images you capture; employment, business, income, and affordability information; collateral and asset details; financial and credit information (including CRB reports we obtain with your authorisation); payment and mobile-money transaction data; device and usage records needed for security (for example login attempts and session data); support and complaint records; and optional marketing preferences where you opt in.'],
            ['Sources of personal data', 'We collect data you provide directly; data generated by your use of the platform; and data from authorised third parties such as national identity services (NIDA), licensed credit reference bureaus (CRB), payment service providers, valuation or recovery partners you engage through our flows, and regulators when they lawfully require or provide information. When we obtain data from third parties for KYC or credit assessment, we use it for the disclosed lending and compliance purposes in this Policy.'],
            ['Device permissions', 'For KYC we request only camera access or files you select through the system file picker. We only use your device camera or the file picker you choose for identity and document photos. We do not access contacts, SMS inbox, call logs, or social media accounts on your device. You may switch between front and back cameras when capturing. Photos are encrypted in transit and reviewed by underwriting where required for your application.'],
            ['Consents in product', 'At profile and application time you may be asked to authorise NIDA verification, credit-bureau (CRB) checks, and face verification. Those in-product consents form part of this Policy for the purposes stated when you tick or accept them. Refusing a required consent may mean we cannot complete KYC, underwriting, or disbursement for that product.'],
            ['Purposes of processing', 'We process data to: create, authenticate, and secure accounts (including PIN and security questions); verify identity and prevent fraud or impersonation; assess credit and AML risk and make lending decisions; service loans and membership (including schedules, arrears, restructuring, and guarantor/group obligations); send transactional messages (OTP, USSD prompts, e-receipts, repayment reminders, and statutory notices); engage licensed partners for valuation, insurance, collateral, field, or recovery work you authorise; meet regulatory reporting and audit duties; handle complaints and support; and improve service safety. Marketing communications are sent only where allowed and you may opt out of direct marketing.'],
            ['Disclosure and sharing', 'We share personal data only as needed with: licensed payment service providers; credit reference bureaus; identity providers (including NIDA-related services); loan-related partners (for example valuers, insurers, collateral yards, field and recovery agents under fair-collection rules); group leaders or co-members where the product requires shared visibility; and regulators or competent authorities when required by law. Infrastructure and software vendors process data under confidentiality and data-protection terms. We do not sell personal data.'],
            ['Data residency and transborder flow', 'Borrower and member personal data for our Tanzania licensed entity is intended to be hosted and primarily processed in systems supporting operations in the United Republic of Tanzania. Limited overseas access may occur only for maintenance, cloud infrastructure, or licensed processors under confidentiality and data-protection terms consistent with PDPA Parts V–VI (transborder flow). Transfers to a state with adequate protection follow the Act; transfers to a state without adequate protection are made only where the PDPA and Collection and Processing Regulations allow (including PDPC permission where required).'],
            ['Retention and disposal', 'We retain personal data for the life of your relationship with us and for statutory, accounting, credit-reporting, AML, and dispute-resolution periods that apply to microfinance providers. When data is no longer required for those purposes, we delete, destroy, or anonymise it where feasible, and we take steps so that deleted or anonymised data is not casually re-identified.'],
            ['Security measures', 'We use access controls, role-based staff permissions, encryption in transit, PIN/password protections, session controls, and monitoring for misuse. Staff and processors are bound to confidentiality. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure; you must also protect your PIN, password, OTP codes, and devices and notify Support if you suspect unauthorised access.'],
            ['Data Protection Officer', 'A Data Protection Officer (DPO) is charged with helping us comply with the PDPA. The named DPO contact will be published on this page once appointed and registered as required. Until then, privacy and data-subject requests should be sent to :email (subject line: “PDPA / data request”).'],
            ['Automated decisions', 'Credit decisions may use automated scoring together with human underwriting review. Under the PDPA you may request information about significant solely automated decisions that affect you and, where the Act requires, seek human intervention or express your point of view.'],
            ['Your rights under PDPA', 'Subject to the PDPA (Parts VI) and the Collection and Processing Regulations, you may: (a) request access to your personal data; (b) request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data; (c) request rectification, blocking, erasure, or destruction where the Act allows; (d) object to, or apply to prevent, processing that is likely to cause substantial damage to you or another person; (e) prevent processing of your personal data for direct marketing; (f) exercise rights in relation to automated decision-making; and (g) seek compensation where the Act provides for it. Rights are not absolute — we may refuse or limit a request where the PDPA or other law permits (for example ongoing loan, AML, or legal hold obligations).'],
            ['How to exercise your rights', 'Send a clear request to Support or :email with your full name, registered phone, member number (if any), and what you want (access, correction, erasure, objection, marketing opt-out, or automated-decision information). We may need to verify your identity before acting. We aim to respond within a reasonable time consistent with the PDPA and our complaints handling process.'],
            ['Complaints to the PDPC', 'If you consider that there is a violation of personal data protection principles, or you are dissatisfied with our decision on a data request, you may lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection Commission (PDPC) under the Personal Data Protection (Complaints Settlement Procedures) Regulations, 2023 (including Form No. 1 as provided by the Commission). You may also use our Complaints policy and :email first so we can try to resolve the matter quickly.'],
